es/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#using-the-dashboard","content":"Using the Dashboard"},"2935":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dns-provider-examples","content":"DNS Provider Examples"},"2936":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#cloudflare","content":"Cloudflare"},"2937":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-23","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#amazon-route-53","content":"Amazon Route 53"},"2938":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-24","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#godaddy","content":"GoDaddy"},"2939":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-25","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"2940":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-26","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dns-propagation-delays","content":"DNS propagation delays"},"2941":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-27","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#conflicting-spf-records","content":"Conflicting SPF records"},"2942":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-28","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#too-many-dns-lookups-spf-error","content":"\"Too many DNS lookups\" SPF error"},"2943":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-29","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dkim-record-not-found","content":"DKIM record not found"},"2944":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-30","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dmarc-reports-not-arriving","content":"DMARC reports not arriving"},"2945":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-31","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dns-setup-guide","content":"Properly configured DNS records are essential for email deliverability. Without them, your emails are far more likely to land in spam or be rejected outright. This guide covers the three key authentication records (SPF, DKIM, DMARC) and the optional MX record for inbox users."},"2946":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-32","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"Email authentication works through DNS records that prove you authorized NorthRelay to send email on behalf of your domain. Receiving mail servers check these records to verify legitimacy."},"2947":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-33","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"| Record  | Purpose                                                          | Required |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| **SPF** | Declares which servers are allowed to send email for your domain | Yes      |","table":"table-0"},"2948":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"| Record   | Purpose                                                                 | Required              |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| **DKIM** | Adds a cryptographic signature to prove the email was not tampered with | Yes (auto-configured) |","table":"table-0"},"2949":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"| Record    | Purpose                                                                  | Required             |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------- |\n| **DMARC** | Tells receiving servers what to do with emails that fail SPF/DKIM checks | Strongly recommended |","table":"table-0"},"2950":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#overview","content":"| Record | Purpose                                                                 | Required       |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| **MX** | Routes inbound email to NorthRelay's mailbox servers (inbox users only) | Only for inbox |","table":"table-0"},"2951":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-37","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#spf-record","content":"SPF (Sender Policy Framework) tells receiving mail servers which IP addresses are authorized to send email for your domain."},"2952":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-38","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"Add a TXT record at the root of your domain:"},"2953":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-39","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"| Field    | Value |\n| -------- | ----- |\n| **Type** | TXT   |","table":"table-1"},"2954":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-40","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"| Field         | Value                                                |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Host/Name** | `@` (or leave blank, depending on your DNS provider) |","table":"table-1"},"2955":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-41","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"| Field     | Value                                    |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **Value** | `v=spf1 include:_spf.north-pipe.ca -all` |","table":"table-1"},"2956":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-42","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add","content":"| Field   | Value             |\n| ------- | ----------------- |\n| **TTL** | 3600 (or default) |","table":"table-1"},"2957":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-43","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#how-it-works","content":"The `include:_spf.north-pipe.ca` directive tells receiving servers to look up NorthRelay's SPF record, which lists NorthRelay's sending IPs (IPv4 and IPv6), so you never need to update SPF when our infrastructure changes. The `-all` suffix means \"reject email from any other source\" — this is the strictest and most secure setting."},"2958":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#if-you-already-have-an-spf-record","content":"A domain can only have **one** SPF TXT record. If you already send email through another provider, merge the records:"},"2959":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#if-you-already-have-an-spf-record","content":"Do not create a second TXT record starting with `v=spf1` — this will cause SPF to fail entirely."},"2960":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Using `~all` (softfail) instead of `-all` (hardfail) — softfail is weaker and may not protect you"},"2961":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Adding more than 10 DNS lookups in your SPF chain (SPF has a 10-lookup limit)"},"2962":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Creating multiple SPF records on the same domain"},"2963":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-49","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#common-mistakes","content":"Existing domains using `include:north-pipe.ca` remain supported. New setup instructions use `include:_spf.north-pipe.ca`. Publish only one SPF record."},"2964":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-50","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dkim-record","content":"DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) adds a cryptographic signature to each outgoing email, allowing the recipient to verify the message was not altered in transit."},"2965":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-51","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#configure-your-domain","content":"For a custom domain, publish the DKIM TXT record shown in Domains & senders at `default._domainkey.yourdomain.com`. Copy the full signing key from the dashboard. NorthRelay manages the signing infrastructure; you manage DNS for your custom domain. Managed NorthRelay domains are configured automatically."},"2966":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-52","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#configure-your-domain","content":"To verify your domain:"},"2967":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-53","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#configure-your-domain","content":"Go to **Dashboard → Domains**"},"2968":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-54","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#configure-your-domain","content":"Click **Add Domain** and enter your domain name"},"2969":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-55","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#configure-your-domain","content":"Add the per-domain ownership TXT record at `_northrelay.yourdomain.com`, plus the SPF and DKIM TXT records shown in the dashboard"},"2970":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-56","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#configure-your-domain","content":"Click **Verify**"},"2971":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-57","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#configure-your-domain","content":"Once verified, DKIM signing is enabled automatically"},"2972":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-58","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#verifying-dkim","content":"After domain verification, confirm the DKIM record is published:"},"2973":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-59","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#verifying-dkim","content":"You should see a response containing a `v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=...` value. If the record is missing, wait up to 48 hours for DNS propagation, then check again."},"2974":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-60","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#subdomains","content":"DKIM signing supports subdomains automatically. If you send from `notifications@sub.yourdomain.com`, the parent domain's DKIM key will sign the email (using the `SubDomains=yes` configuration on NorthRelay's signing infrastructure)."},"2975":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-61","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dmarc-record","content":"DMARC (Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance) tells receiving servers how to handle emails that fail SPF or DKIM checks, and where to send aggregate reports."},"2976":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-62","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"Add a TXT record at `_dmarc.yourdomain.com`:"},"2977":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-63","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"| Field    | Value |\n| -------- | ----- |\n| **Type** | TXT   |","table":"table-2"},"2978":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-64","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"| Field         | Value    |\n| ------------- | -------- |\n| **Host/Name** | `_dmarc` |","table":"table-2"},"2979":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-65","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"| Field     | Value                                                     |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Value** | `v=DMARC1; p=quarantine; rua=mailto:dmarc@yourdomain.com` |","table":"table-2"},"2980":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-66","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#what-to-add-1","content":"| Field   | Value             |\n| ------- | ----------------- |\n| **TTL** | 3600 (or default) |","table":"table-2"},"2981":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-67","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#policy-options","content":"| Policy   | Behavior                     | Recommended When                                 |\n| -------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `p=none` | Monitor only, take no action | Initial setup — use this while reviewing reports |","table":"table-3"},"2982":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-68","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#policy-options","content":"| Policy         | Behavior                    | Recommended When                          |\n| -------------- | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `p=quarantine` | Send failing emails to spam | After confirming SPF and DKIM are working |","table":"table-3"},"2983":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-69","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#policy-options","content":"| Policy     | Behavior                       | Recommended When                                         |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `p=reject` | Reject failing emails outright | Maximum protection, once you are confident in your setup |","table":"table-3"},"2984":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-70","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#policy-options","content":"We recommend starting with `p=quarantine` and moving to `p=reject` after monitoring reports for 2-4 weeks."},"2985":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-71","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#full-dmarc-record-example","content":"| Tag            | Meaning                                    |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `p=quarantine` | Quarantine emails that fail authentication |","table":"table-4"},"2986":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-72","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#full-dmarc-record-example","content":"| Tag             | Meaning                    |\n| --------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `sp=quarantine` | Same policy for subdomains |","table":"table-4"},"2987":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-73","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#full-dmarc-record-example","content":"| Tag              | Meaning                                           |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rua=mailto:...` | Where to send aggregate reports (daily summaries) |","table":"table-4"},"2988":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-74","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#full-dmarc-record-example","content":"| Tag              | Meaning                                              |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ruf=mailto:...` | Where to send forensic reports (individual failures) |","table":"table-4"},"2989":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-75","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#full-dmarc-record-example","content":"| Tag       | Meaning                                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `adkim=r` | Relaxed DKIM alignment (allows subdomain signing) |","table":"table-4"},"2990":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-76","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#full-dmarc-record-example","content":"| Tag      | Meaning               |\n| -------- | --------------------- |\n| `aspf=r` | Relaxed SPF alignment |","table":"table-4"},"2991":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-77","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#full-dmarc-record-example","content":"| Tag       | Meaning                                |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `pct=100` | Apply policy to 100% of failing emails |","table":"table-4"},"2992":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-78","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#mx-record-inbox-users","content":"If you are on the **Pro** tier or above and want to receive email through NorthRelay's inbox, add an MX record pointing to NorthRelay's mailbox server."},"2993":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-79","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#mx-record-inbox-users","content":"| Field    | Value |\n| -------- | ----- |\n| **Type** | MX    |","table":"table-5"},"2994":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-80","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#mx-record-inbox-users","content":"| Field         | Value                |\n| ------------- | -------------------- |\n| **Host/Name** | `@` (or leave blank) |","table":"table-5"},"2995":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-81","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#mx-record-inbox-users","content":"| Field     | Value              |\n| --------- | ------------------ |\n| **Value** | `mx.northrelay.ca` |","table":"table-5"},"2996":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-82","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#mx-record-inbox-users","content":"| Field        | Value |\n| ------------ | ----- |\n| **Priority** | `10`  |","table":"table-5"},"2997":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-83","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#mx-record-inbox-users","content":"| Field   | Value             |\n| ------- | ----------------- |\n| **TTL** | 3600 (or default) |","table":"table-5"},"2998":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-84","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#mx-record-inbox-users","content":"This routes inbound email for your domain to NorthRelay's mailbox servers, where it is accessible via the Dashboard inbox or IMAP/JMAP clients."},"2999":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-85","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#using-the-dashboard","content":"Go to **Dashboard → Domains**, select your domain, and click **Check DNS**. The dashboard will verify all required records and report any issues."},"3000":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-86","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#cloudflare","content":"Log in to Cloudflare and select your domain"},"3001":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-87","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#cloudflare","content":"Go to **DNS → Records → Add Record**"},"3002":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-88","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#cloudflare","content":"Set type to **TXT**, name to `@`, and paste the SPF value"},"3003":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-89","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#cloudflare","content":"Repeat for DMARC (name: `_dmarc`)"},"3004":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-90","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#cloudflare","content":"If using proxy (orange cloud), note that TXT records are never proxied"},"3005":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-91","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#amazon-route-53","content":"Open the Route 53 console and select your hosted zone"},"3006":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-92","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#amazon-route-53","content":"Click **Create Record**"},"3007":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-93","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#amazon-route-53","content":"Leave the record name blank for root, set type to **TXT**"},"3008":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-94","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#amazon-route-53","content":"Paste the SPF value in quotes: `\"v=spf1 include:_spf.north-pipe.ca -all\"`"},"3009":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-95","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#amazon-route-53","content":"Route 53 requires TXT values to be enclosed in double quotes"},"3010":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-96","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#godaddy","content":"Go to **My Products → DNS** for your domain"},"3011":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-97","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#godaddy","content":"Click **Add** under the Records section"},"3012":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-98","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#godaddy","content":"Select type **TXT**, set host to `@`, and paste the SPF value"},"3013":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-99","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#godaddy","content":"GoDaddy may take up to 48 hours to propagate changes"},"3014":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-100","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dns-propagation-delays","content":"DNS changes can take up to **48 hours** to propagate globally, though most providers update within 1-4 hours."},"3015":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-101","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dns-propagation-delays","content":"Use dnschecker.org to check propagation status worldwide"},"3016":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-102","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dns-propagation-delays","content":"Lower your TTL to 300 (5 minutes) before making changes to speed up future updates"},"3017":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-103","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#conflicting-spf-records","content":"If you have multiple TXT records starting with `v=spf1`, SPF validation will fail. Merge all `include:` directives into a single record."},"3018":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-104","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#too-many-dns-lookups-spf-error","content":"SPF allows a maximum of 10 DNS lookups. Each `include:` directive counts as one lookup. If you exceed 10, consider:"},"3019":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-105","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#too-many-dns-lookups-spf-error","content":"Removing providers you no longer use"},"3020":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-106","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#too-many-dns-lookups-spf-error","content":"Using `ip4:` or `ip6:` directives instead of `include:` for static IPs"},"3021":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-107","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#too-many-dns-lookups-spf-error","content":"Using an SPF flattening service"},"3022":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-108","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dkim-record-not-found","content":"Wait up to 48 hours after domain verification"},"3023":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-109","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dkim-record-not-found","content":"Confirm you verified the domain in **Dashboard → Domains**"},"3024":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-110","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dkim-record-not-found","content":"Check the exact record name: `default._domainkey.yourdomain.com` (not `dkim._domainkey`)"},"3025":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-111","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dmarc-reports-not-arriving","content":"Verify the `rua` email address is correct and can receive email"},"3026":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-112","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dmarc-reports-not-arriving","content":"Some providers take 24-48 hours to start sending reports"},"3027":{"id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup-113","page_id":"/docs/guides/dns-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/dns-setup#dmarc-reports-not-arriving","content":"Check that the `rua` address domain has a DMARC report authorization record if it differs from the sending domain"},"3028":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"page","content":"Mailing Lists and Newsletters","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists"},"3029":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","content":"Build newsletter signup, double opt-in, a preference page and unsubscribe handling in your own app on top of NorthRelay."},"3030":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-1","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#mailing-lists-and-newsletters","content":"Mailing Lists and Newsletters"},"3031":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-2","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"The building blocks"},"3032":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-3","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#1-set-up-a-topic-and-a-list","content":"1. Set up a topic and a list"},"3033":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-4","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"2. Collect signups"},"3034":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-5","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"Subscribing from your backend"},"3035":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-6","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"3. Double opt-in"},"3036":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-7","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"4. Keep consent evidence (CASL and GDPR)"},"3037":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-8","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"5. A preference page inside your product"},"3038":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-9","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"6. Unsubscribe links and one-click unsubscribe"},"3039":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-10","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"7. Hosting your own unsubscribe page"},"3040":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-11","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"8. Keep your app in sync with webhooks"},"3041":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-12","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"9. Import an existing list"},"3042":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-13","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"10. Bounce and complaint protection"},"3043":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-14","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Checklist"},"3044":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-15","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#related","content":"Related"},"3045":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-16","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#mailing-lists-and-newsletters","content":"This guide shows how to build mailing-list features into your own product with NorthRelay: a newsletter signup, double opt-in, a preference page inside your app, unsubscribe links, and keeping your database in sync. NorthRelay holds the audience and enforces the opt-out rules; your app calls the API and listens to webhooks."},"3046":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-17","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#mailing-lists-and-newsletters","content":"You need an API key with `contacts:read` and `contacts:write` (and `suppressions:write` if you create topics through the API). Campaigns are available on Micro and above; lists, contacts and the Subscriptions API work on every plan. On Free, subscriptions and signup forms can activate up to 100 contacts."},"3047":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-18","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"| Concept     | What it means                                                                                                                                     | API      |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| **Contact** | One recipient address in your account, with status (`PENDING`, `ACTIVE`, `UNSUBSCRIBED`, `BOUNCED`, `COMPLAINED`, `CLEANED`) and consent evidence | Contacts |","table":"table-0"},"3048":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-19","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"| Concept  | What it means                                                   | API           |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| **List** | An audience you send campaigns to, such as \"Monthly newsletter\" | Contact lists |","table":"table-0"},"3049":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-20","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"| Concept   | What it means                                                                                                                                                         | API    |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------ |\n| **Topic** | A kind of mail people can opt out of on its own, such as \"Product updates\" or \"Events\". Stored as a suppression group whose members are the people who **opted out**. | Topics |","table":"table-0"},"3050":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-21","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"| Concept                | What it means                                                                                                      | API           |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------- |\n| **Global unsubscribe** | \"Stop all marketing mail.\" Contact becomes `UNSUBSCRIBED` and an account-level `Unsubscribe` suppression is added. | Subscriptions |","table":"table-0"},"3051":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-22","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"**Lists or topics?** Use a list for \"who do I send this to\" and a topic for \"what kind of mail is this\". A common setup is one topic per kind of mail, and each list tagged with its topic. Then:"},"3052":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-23","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"opting out of the topic removes the person from every list tagged with it, and"},"3053":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-24","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"any marketing send under that topic (a campaign to a tagged list, a campaign with that subscription topic, or a marketing-stream API send with `suppressionGroupId`) skips people who opted out, whichever list they are on."},"3054":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-25","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#the-building-blocks","content":"Campaigns go only to current members of the list: someone who unsubscribed from the list (`scope: \"list\"`) or has not yet confirmed a double opt-in (`PENDING`) is not sent the campaign. Tag your lists with topics as well, so that one opt-out covers every list and every send of that kind of mail."},"3055":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-26","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#1-set-up-a-topic-and-a-list","content":"Create the topic, give it the wording recipients will see, and create a list tagged with it."},"3056":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-27","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#1-set-up-a-topic-and-a-list","content":"You can do the same in the dashboard under Contacts."},"3057":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-28","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"There are two ways to get people onto a list."},"3058":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-29","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"|               | Hosted signup form                                                                    | Subscriptions API                                                |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Where it runs | Browser posts straight to NorthRelay (`POST /api/v1/forms/{id}/submit`, public, CORS) | Your server calls `POST /api/v1/subscriptions` with your API key |","table":"table-1"},"3059":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-30","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"|          | Hosted signup form                         | Subscriptions API                                               |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Best for | Marketing sites, landing pages, no backend | Signups inside your product, checkout opt-ins, account settings |","table":"table-1"},"3060":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-31","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"|                 | Hosted signup form                                                          | Subscriptions API                |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Spam protection | Honeypot field, allowed origins, rate limits, optional Cloudflare Turnstile | Yours (you control the endpoint) |","table":"table-1"},"3061":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-32","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"|               | Hosted signup form | Subscriptions API                                |\n| ------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Double opt-in | Per-form setting   | `doubleOptIn: true` per call, with `redirectUrl` |","table":"table-1"},"3062":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-33","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"|                  | Hosted signup form                                                                                                              | Subscriptions API                                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Consent evidence | Stored on the contact automatically: source `form`, time, submission IP and user agent, and the text `Signup form: <form name>` | `consent.ip`, `consent.userAgent`, `consent.text` you pass, stored on the contact with source `api` |","table":"table-1"},"3063":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-34","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"|        | Hosted signup form              | Subscriptions API            |\n| ------ | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Topics | The form's list (and its topic) | Any `listIds` and `topicIds` |","table":"table-1"},"3064":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-35","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#2-collect-signups","content":"Never put your API key in browser code. If the signup happens in the browser and you want the API's features, post to your own backend and call the API from there."},"3065":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-36","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"In Python (`northrelay` 1.9.0 is async):"},"3066":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-37","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"Or with `curl`:"},"3067":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-38","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"The call is idempotent: calling it again for someone already on the list returns `200` and adds nothing."},"3068":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-39","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"Handle these errors in your signup handler:"},"3069":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-40","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"| Code                     | What to tell the user                                                                                                                           |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `RECIPIENT_UNSUBSCRIBED` | They unsubscribed earlier. If they are signing up again now, that is fresh consent: retry with `\"resubscribe\": true` and `\"doubleOptIn\": true`. |","table":"table-2"},"3070":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-41","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"| Code                   | What to tell the user                                              |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `RECIPIENT_SUPPRESSED` | The address bounced or reported spam. Ask for a different address. |","table":"table-2"},"3071":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-42","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"| Code              | What to tell the user                                           |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CONTACT_BLOCKED` | Same as above; this address cannot be re-added through the API. |","table":"table-2"},"3072":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-43","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#subscribing-from-your-backend","content":"| Code                      | What to tell the user                                   |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `FREE_TIER_CONTACT_LIMIT` | Your account is at its contact limit; upgrade the plan. |","table":"table-2"},"3073":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-44","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"With `doubleOptIn: true`:"},"3074":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-45","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"The contact is created as `PENDING` and added to the lists. Campaigns skip it while it is `PENDING`."},"3075":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-46","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"NorthRelay emails a confirmation link (`https://app.northrelay.ca/c/<token>`, valid for 7 days). Pass `confirmationTemplateId` to use your own template; it can use `{{confirm_url}}`, `{{first_name}}`, `{{last_name}}` and `{{email}}`."},"3076":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-47","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"The recipient clicks; the contact becomes `ACTIVE`, the `contact.confirmed` webhook fires, and the browser is redirected to your `redirectUrl` (`https://` only)."},"3077":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-48","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"If someone says the email never arrived, call `POST /api/v1/subscriptions/{email}/resend-confirmation`. It re-sends the email and gives the link another 7 days."},"3078":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-49","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#3-double-opt-in","content":"Double opt-in is the strongest consent record you can have, and it keeps typos and bots off your list, which protects your deliverability. Use it for anything public-facing."},"3079":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-50","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"Canada's anti-spam law (CASL) and the EU's GDPR expect you to show when and how each person agreed to receive marketing mail. For every API subscribe call and every signup form submission, NorthRelay stores on the contact:"},"3080":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-51","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"| Field           | Source                                                            |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `consentSource` | How they subscribed: `api`, `form`, `import`, `preference_center` |","table":"table-3"},"3081":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-52","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"| Field       | Source |\n| ----------- | ------ |\n| `consentAt` | When   |","table":"table-3"},"3082":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-53","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"| Field                           | Source                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `consentIp`, `consentUserAgent` | What you passed in `consent` (signup forms record the submitting browser) |","table":"table-3"},"3083":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-54","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"| Field         | Source                                                                      |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `consentText` | The wording they agreed to (signup forms record `Signup form: <form name>`) |","table":"table-3"},"3084":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-55","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"| Field         | Source                                |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `confirmedAt` | When they confirmed the double opt-in |","table":"table-3"},"3085":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-56","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"Pass `consent.text` with the exact label of the checkbox or button the person used, and pass their IP from your server (NorthRelay only sees your server's address). Read it back at any time:"},"3086":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-57","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#4-keep-consent-evidence-casl-and-gdpr","content":"This guide is not legal advice; check what your jurisdiction and audience require."},"3087":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-58","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"Let signed-in users manage their email from your own settings screen. Read the current state with `GET /subscriptions/{email}` and save their choices with `PATCH /subscriptions/{email}`."},"3088":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-59","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"Render a checkbox per topic (use `label` and `description`, falling back to `name`), and a \"Unsubscribe from all marketing email\" option. On save, send only what changed:"},"3089":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-60","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"Things to know:"},"3090":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-61","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"`GET` returns `200` with `contact: null` for someone who never subscribed, so the page works for every user."},"3091":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-62","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"`topics` lists every topic in your account. If some are internal, filter them out."},"3092":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-63","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#5-a-preference-page-inside-your-product","content":"Turning a topic back on does not undo \"unsubscribe from all\". To bring someone back, the user has to opt in again; then call `POST /subscriptions` (or `PATCH` with `lists`) with `\"resubscribe\": true` and fresh `consent`."},"3093":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-64","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"Every marketing message needs a working unsubscribe link, and Gmail, Yahoo and Outlook require RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe headers for bulk senders. NorthRelay handles both:"},"3094":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-65","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"**Campaigns:** put `{{unsubscribe_url}}` in your template footer. NorthRelay adds the `List-Unsubscribe` and `List-Unsubscribe-Post: List-Unsubscribe=One-Click` headers to every message."},"3095":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-66","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"**Preference link:** put `{{preferences_url}}` next to it to give recipients a signed link to NorthRelay's hosted preference centre, where they can choose topics or unsubscribe from everything."},"3096":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-67","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"**API mail on a marketing message stream:** NorthRelay injects the unsubscribe footer and the same headers automatically. Unsubscribes from these messages are attributed to your account and fire `contact.unsubscribed`, even when the recipient is not one of your contacts."},"3097":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-68","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#6-unsubscribe-links-and-one-click-unsubscribe","content":"When a mailbox provider's \"Unsubscribe\" button is pressed, NorthRelay unsubscribes the recipient from all marketing mail and fires `contact.unsubscribed` with `method: \"one_click\"`. A plain `GET` of the one-click URL never unsubscribes anyone, because security scanners prefetch links."},"3098":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-69","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"NorthRelay's hosted unsubscribe and preference pages work out of the box. If you would rather keep recipients on your own domain for campaign mail, link to your page and pass along the NorthRelay link:"},"3099":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-70","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"The unsubscribe link has the form `https://track.north-pipe.ca/u/{token}`. Your page takes the last path segment as the token, asks the recipient what they want, and posts it to the public endpoint (no API key; the token is the authentication):"},"3100":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-71","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"Notes:"},"3101":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-72","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"Tokens are signed and expire. `INVALID_TOKEN` means the link is too old or was altered."},"3102":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-73","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"The page must not unsubscribe on page load (link scanners open it). Do it when the recipient presses a button."},"3103":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-74","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"The `List-Unsubscribe` header still points at NorthRelay, so one-click from the mailbox provider keeps working without your page."},"3104":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-75","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#7-hosting-your-own-unsubscribe-page","content":"For opt-outs made by a signed-in user in your product, skip the token and call `POST /api/v1/subscriptions/unsubscribe` from your server with your API key."},"3105":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-76","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Register one webhook endpoint for the contact and list events, and optionally engagement events:"},"3106":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-77","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"| Event                | Typical use                                                               |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contact.subscribed` | Mark the user as \"newsletter: pending\" or \"subscribed\" (`details.status`) |","table":"table-4"},"3107":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-78","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"| Event               | Typical use                                                      |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contact.confirmed` | Flip \"pending\" to \"subscribed\"; send a welcome email or a coupon |","table":"table-4"},"3108":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-79","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"| Event                  | Typical use                                                                           |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contact.unsubscribed` | Turn off the matching setting in your app (`details.scope`: `all`, `list` or `topic`) |","table":"table-4"},"3109":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-80","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"| Event                                       | Typical use                                      |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `list.member_added` / `list.member_removed` | Mirror list membership if you show it in your UI |","table":"table-4"},"3110":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-81","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"| Event                            | Typical use                                                                          |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `email.opened` / `email.clicked` | Engagement scoring, \"last seen\" in your CRM. Human activity only; bots are filtered. |","table":"table-4"},"3111":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-82","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"| Event           | Typical use                          |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `email.bounced` | Ask the user to update their address |","table":"table-4"},"3112":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-83","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"A minimal handler:"},"3113":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-84","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"The Python SDK has a `WebhookPayload` model (`event_type`, `message_id`, `timestamp`, `recipient`, `details`); verify the signature with `hmac.compare_digest` over the raw body first, as shown in the Webhooks reference."},"3114":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-85","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#8-keep-your-app-in-sync-with-webhooks","content":"Respond within 10 seconds and do slow work asynchronously. Payload details are in the Webhooks reference."},"3115":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-86","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Moving from another provider? Import the CSV straight into a list:"},"3116":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-87","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"The response reports `imported`, `skipped` (already existed), `addedToList` and per-row `errors`. Each request takes up to 1,000 rows and 2 MiB; split larger files."},"3117":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-88","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"With the SDKs:"},"3118":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-89","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Before importing:"},"3119":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-90","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Only import people who opted in to your mail. Imported contacts are recorded with consent source `import`."},"3120":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-91","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Import your old provider's unsubscribes, bounces and complaints as suppressions first (`POST /api/v1/suppressions/bulk` with `reason` `Unsubscribe`, `Bounce` or `Complaint`), so they are never mailed."},"3121":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-92","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#9-import-an-existing-list","content":"Imports do not fire webhooks. Sync your app from your source data, not from webhooks, for the initial load."},"3122":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-93","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"NorthRelay protects your sender reputation, and the shared sending IP, automatically:"},"3123":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-94","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"A hard bounce adds a `Bounce` suppression; a spam complaint adds a `Complaint` suppression. Neither is ever lifted by a subscribe call, and both block even transactional mail."},"3124":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-95","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"Marketing sends also skip anyone who unsubscribed from everything or opted out of the topic the mail is sent under, and campaigns skip members who left the list or have not confirmed their double opt-in."},"3125":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-96","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"Adding an existing contact to a list does not make it mailable again: suppressed and unsubscribed members stay in the list but are skipped at send time and shown with `suppressionStatuses` in `GET /contacts/lists/{id}/members`."},"3126":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-97","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"Suppressed recipients are dropped before quota is counted."},"3127":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-98","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#10-bounce-and-complaint-protection","content":"Keep complaint rates low by using double opt-in, sending what people signed up for, putting the preference and unsubscribe links where they are easy to find, and removing people who have not engaged in a long time."},"3128":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-99","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Topics created, with public labels, and each list tagged with its topic"},"3129":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-100","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Signup calls `POST /subscriptions` from your server with `doubleOptIn`, `redirectUrl` and `consent`"},"3130":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-101","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Signup handler handles `RECIPIENT_UNSUBSCRIBED` and `RECIPIENT_SUPPRESSED`"},"3131":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-102","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Campaign templates include `{{unsubscribe_url}}` and `{{preferences_url}}`"},"3132":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-103","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Preference page uses `GET` and `PATCH /subscriptions/{email}`"},"3133":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-104","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Webhook endpoint verifies signatures and handles `contact.*` events"},"3134":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-105","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#checklist","content":"Old provider's suppressions imported before the contacts"},"3135":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-106","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#related","content":"Subscriptions API"},"3136":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-107","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#related","content":"Contacts API"},"3137":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-108","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#related","content":"Suppressions API"},"3138":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-109","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#related","content":"Webhooks"},"3139":{"id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists-110","page_id":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/mailing-lists#related","content":"TypeScript SDK · Python SDK · MCP Server"},"3140":{"id":"/docs/guides/nodejs-integration","page_id":"/docs/guides/nodejs-integration","type":"page","content":"Node.js Integration","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/guides/nodejs-integration"},"3141":{"id":"/docs/guides/nodejs-integration-0","page_id":"/docs/guides/nodejs-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/nodejs-integration","content":"Send emails from Node.js applications using Nodemail