rl":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#current-hosted-mailbox-deployment","content":"The hosted mailbox service runs Stalwart Community 0.16.23 on the former shared\nrelay host, with native JMAP administration. Client access is documented in\nHosted email access. The deployment source is the\nplatform repository's `infra/mailbox-next` directory."},"3812":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-33","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#current-hosted-mailbox-deployment","content":"The generic split-role examples below also describe the separately versioned\napplication sending instance. Do not apply an old SQL-directory configuration\nor `/api/principal` management example to the 0.16 production mailbox. Mailbox\nadministration uses native `x:Account/*`, `x:Domain/*` and `x:AppPassword/*` methods."},"3813":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"Stalwart Mail Server is a modern, Rust-based mail server distributed as a single binary. It supports SMTP, IMAP, JMAP, and includes built-in spam filtering, DKIM, and a management API."},"3814":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"NorthRelay uses Stalwart in a **split-role architecture** with two separate instances:"},"3815":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"| Instance           | Role            | Location      | Purpose                                                              |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Outbound Relay** | Queue + routing | Sanc