t","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Routes every email, on every tier, to the single sending relay (`sovereign.north-pipe.ca`)"},"3823":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"DKIM signing is **disabled** (handled by OpenDKIM on relay VPSes)"},"3824":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Management API on port 8080 (internal only)"},"3825":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"The mailbox instance handles all inbound email and user inbox access:"},"3826":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Key characteristics:"},"3827":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Runs on a dedicated Mailbox VPS"},"3828":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-49","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"MX records point here (`mx.northrelay.ca`)"},"3829":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-50","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Provides IMAP and JMAP access for dashboard inbox"},"3830":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-51","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Uses SQL directory queries against PostgreSQL for authentication"},"3831":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-52","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Each user's inbox email = their subdomain slot email"},"3832":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-53","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#toml-configuration-basics","content":"Stalwart's static configuration uses TOML format. Key sections:"},"3833":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-54","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#authentication","content":"The `fallback-admin.secret` is the token used for Management API and CLI authentication."},"3834":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-55","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#queue-and-routing","content":"See Outbound routing below for the details."},"3835":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-56","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#management-api","content":"The Management API runs on port 8080 and provides HTTP endpoints for administration."},"3836":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-57","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#authentication-1","content":"All API requests require authentication:"},"3837":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-58","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#cli-tool","content":"The Stalwart CLI (`stalwart-cli`) manages runtime configuration stored in RocksDB."},"3838":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-59","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#ip-blocking-prevention","content":"> **This is the most common operational issue with Stalwart.**"},"3839":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-60","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#ip-blocking-prevention","content":"Stalwart has an auto-ban feature that blocks IP addresses after failed authentication attempts. Blocked IPs are stored in **RocksDB** (not the TOML config), so they persist across restarts."},"3840":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-61","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"SMTP connection closes immediately without a banner"},"3841":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-62","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"Telnet to port 25 connects then disconnects instantly"},"3842":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-63","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"No error in application logs - the connection is dropped at the Stalwart level"},"3843":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-64","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#prevention","content":"Add trusted IPs to the allowlist in your TOML config:"},"3844":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-65","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#prevention","content":"Or disable auto-ban entirely for development:"},"3845":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-66","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#sql-directory-queries","content":"The mailbox Stalwart instance uses SQL queries against PostgreSQL for user authentication and mail routing. These queries are stored in RocksDB and queried at runtime."},"3846":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-67","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query        | Purpose                                    | Supports Catch-All |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------ |\n| `recipients` | Determine if an address should be accepted | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3847":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-68","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query  | Purpose                                | Supports Catch-All |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `name` | Resolve a user account from an address | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3848":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-69","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query    | Purpose                                     | Supports Catch-All |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `emails` | Get all allowed sender addresses for a user | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3849":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-70","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query     | Purpose                              | Supports Catch-All |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------ |\n| `secrets` | Get password hash for authentication | No                 |","table":"table-1"},"3850":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-71","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query     | Purpose                 | Supports Catch-All |\n| --------- | ----------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `members` | Group membership lookup | No                 |","table":"table-1"},"3851":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-72","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#catch-all-support","content":"The `recipients` and `name` queries include catch-all logic: if no exact match is found, they check whether the domain has `is_inbox_hosted = true` in the `domains` table. If so, all mail to that domain routes to the domain owner."},"3852":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-73","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-management","content":"Stalwart principals represent user accounts. For the mailbox instance, principals are provisioned automatically during user registration."},"3853":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-74","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field  | Description                    |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ |\n| `type` | `individual` for user accounts |","table":"table-2"},"3854":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-75","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field  | Description                        |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `name` | Primary identifier (usually email) |","table":"table-2"},"3855":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-76","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field    | Description                                                     |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emails` | Array of all email addresses this principal can send/receive as |","table":"table-2"},"3856":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-77","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field     | Description                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `secrets` | Array containing bcrypt password hash |","table":"table-2"},"3857":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-78","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field   | Description                                 |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `quota` | Mailbox size limit in bytes (0 = unlimited) |","table":"table-2"},"3858":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-79","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"The outbound relay sends every message, on every tier, through one route to the sending relay:"},"3859":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-80","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"| Route   | Address                                                   | Relay VPS      |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `relay` | `sovereign.north-pipe.ca:25` (over WireGuard, `10.0.2.2`) | `76.13.27.101` |","table":"table-3"},"3860":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-81","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Rules that matter in Stalwart v0.15:"},"3861":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-82","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"The route address **must be a DNS hostname**, never a raw IP — a raw IP triggers a \"record not found for MX\" error. On Sanctuary, `/etc/hosts` maps `sovereign.north-pipe.ca` to the WireGuard address `10.0.2.2` so the route stays inside the tunnel."},"3862":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-83","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"`queue.outbound.next-hop` is ignored; only `queue.strategy.route` selects the route."},"3863":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-84","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"RocksDB keys override the TOML file. After changing the route, delete any stale `queue.strategy.route` / `queue.route.*` keys and run `server reload-config`."},"3864":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-85","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Never set `queue.outbound.is_local` on the relay instance — it has no mailboxes."},"3865":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-86","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Tier does not affect routing. See Sending Infrastructure for what protects the relay's reputation."},"3866":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-87","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Configuration Guide - Environment variables and service configuration"},"3867":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-88","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Monitoring - Health checks for Stalwart and related services"},"3868":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-89","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Runbooks - Troubleshooting Stalwart issues"},"3869":{"id":"/d